This package vendors component source from Cerner Terra Core
(https://github.com/cerner/terra-core) and Cerner Terra Framework
(https://github.com/cerner/terra-framework) — the latter via its published npm
tarballs, which ship src/ — Copyright Cerner Innovation, Inc., licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0.

terra-date-picker's src/react-datepicker is Cerner's own fork of react-datepicker
(https://github.com/Hacker0x01/react-datepicker, originally MIT, Copyright
HackerOne Inc. and individual contributors). Cerner redistributes it inside
terra-date-picker under Apache-2.0 with no separate notice; it is vendored here
as it ships, as part of that package's source tree.

Both Terra projects were archived in 2024 with peer dependencies pinned to
React 16. The sources under src/vendor are copied and mechanically adapted for
React 19 by scripts/vendor.mjs; component bodies are otherwise unmodified.
Adaptations: defaultProps on function components replaced by an equivalent
wrapper, react-intl / terra-theme-context / react-onclickoutside /
react-lifecycles-compat replaced by local shims, terra-icon imports replaced by
local stubs, string refs and dead IE-era polyfill imports removed, and
writing-direction-scoped CSS extended to match documents that do not set `dir`.

